section+=['','### Missing measurements and evidence limits','','- VM-only execution, isolated in-process planner/verification phases and allocator traffic: NOT MEASURED. Separate compile/verify command medians are not subtracted from an application-run timing.','- Large-function planner amplification: NOT MEASURED. These generators grow loop data/iteration counts, not function-body size; the experiment cannot close a large-function planning concern.','- Original MiniLang lexer/parser source and frozen input manifest were not supplied/identified in the tracked corpus, issues #2030/#2037 or the checked known qualification folder. NOT RUN; no synthetic equivalent is mislabeled MiniLang.','- Repeated mixed scalar/Sequence updates are represented by the existing State5/State10 loops. A separate original mixed-update generator and a Record+nested-Sequence benchmark were not identified: NOT RUN as independent families. Plain nested-Sequence unit fixtures are not substituted for them.','- Peak RSS is observed process memory, including compiler/verifier/runtime and libraries, not total allocated bytes, an aggregate VM heap quota, or a future retained-version memory bound.','- Linux load averages are recorded per invocation; builds and timed runs are sequential. A Linux snapshot during long baseline execution showed only the benchmark as a sustained CPU consumer and no swap pressure. Windows host contention, CPU frequency/thermal state and scheduler noise are uncontrolled. Brief OS background maintenance was observed during builds, before timings; no software installation/update was initiated by this task. Timing ranges and paired reversals are preserved.','','### Answers to the eight decision questions','','1. Persistent SemMap: **yes empirically for the original Map construction workload/range**; do not generalize fitted sublinear slopes into a complexity guarantee.','2. E1/E2 Record+Sequence: **yes empirically**, with baseline/P1 approximately quadratic and P2 nonquadratic on this range, plus State5/10 controls.','3. Existing linear workloads without material regressions: **NO**. No new quadratic trend was established, but repeated constant-factor slowdowns are demonstrated.','4. State5/10 intended fast path: State5 N=100 activation directly tested; timed State5/10 activation counts not exposed by the release CLI. Large-run scaling improvements are observed, direct State10 move counters NOT MEASURED.','5. End-to-end visibility: **YES**, because primary timings are full CLI application runs.','6. Large-function planner overhead: **INCONCLUSIVE / NOT MEASURED**; no attribution from end-to-end deltas.','7. Cumulative Calls: **YES, a reproduced practical blocker** for the original helper-per-byte lex_calls input; MiniLang-specific ceiling remains historical, not independently reproduced here.','8. Supported follow-up: investigate P2 overhead on scalar record updates, sequence reads/pushes, text scanning and Map operations with phase/dispatch profiling. No storage redesign or quota-policy implementation is inferred from timings.','','### Self-hosting and Checkpoint B recommendation','','**Prioritize P3 — a separately approved bounded Calls override contract.** The hard cumulative ceiling still stops the original 32k lex_calls program even after the major copy-amplification fixes. Keep defaults, independent Calls semantics, verifier/capability behavior and accounting unchanged unless OWNER grants a specific contract/implementation GO. The toy workload does not establish the numeric cap required for a real self-hosting compiler; MiniLang evidence is still needed for that decision.','','**P4 follows:** application-mode O1 execution under the same admitted configuration remains a separate contract gap. Standalone O0/O1 pure parity is observed; run-smc cannot supply the application filesystem host/envelope, and this experiment makes no claim about an O1 compiler-workload speedup.','','**Additional VM optimization is evidence-supported, but focused:** repeated P2 penalties deserve a separately scoped profiling/optimization task. Preserve the large Record+Sequence benefit and deterministic counters; avoid another broad representation rewrite without locating the cost. It does not replace the demonstrated need to address the Calls contract.','','Issues #1910, #2030 and #2037 were checked OPEN and were not edited. This evidence advances #2030’s comparative qualification and #2037’s resource decisions; it does not close either issue or establish #1910 self-hosting completion.','','### Final read-only gate','','PASS: active Windows HEAD, tracked diff/status and untracked list match the initial snapshot; all three detached checkouts are clean; frozen input hashes, lockfiles and built binaries match; remote main and isolated origin/main remain 188dec7eddfafaab5926af2d30f528bfe3d89a2c. No repository/GitHub settings, issues, PRs, source, quotas, dependencies or runtime were modified. All checkouts, targets and raw artifacts are retained. No Checkpoint B implementation started.','','**STOP — EVIDENCE READY FOR OWNER REVIEW.**','']
